Concrete module production and processing equipment for check wells Zhengzhou well wall brick module equipment introduction:
Zhengzhou Yixin is a manufacturer specializing in concrete inspection well modular brick machines, inspection well blocks machinery, and modular wall panels for wells, ranging from semi-automatic to fully automated production lines.
Through years of practice and development, we now have a lineup of high-quality equipment and accompanying facilities, mainly focusing on hydraulic, mobile, and fully automated inspection well series.
Concrete module production and processing equipment for inspection wells Zhengzhou site of well wall brick module assembly:
Characteristics and advantages of well concrete module production and processing equipment:
The inspection well brick-making equipment of Yixin is widely applicable to new masonry materials for municipal underground structures such as coal, heat, water, electricity, and gas.
Such as inspection wells, storm inlets, channels, septic tanks, and small structures such as bridge wing walls for drainage and water storage facilities.
The advantage of constructing manholes with concrete modules lies in their modular structure, which has convex and concave grooves on all sides, allowing them to interlock when assembled.
The wall shear resistance of well wall masonry is far superior to that of plain friction bond masonry.
The module has an open structure, with longitudinal holes connected vertically and transverse holes intersecting horizontally after assembly. After pouring the core of the holes, it forms a poured concrete network structure, which serves to provide secondary reinforcement and waterproofing.
The transverse and longitudinal slots in the modules provide reinforcement bars, while the horizontal tie bars and longitudinal reinforcing bars increase the overall structural strength.
Another type of inspection wells and drainage wells constructed using concrete check-in modules are less likely to experience collapse, subsidence, leakage, among other issues. The mechanical properties of the well walls are stable, operation is simple, and the formed dimensions are standardized.
The concrete check valve mold brick machine equipped with smart control features a data input/output device for an all-in-one touch screen LCD display to monitor the entire mechanical operation process. It achieves ideal human-machine dialogue, automatic material analysis, density operation, safety logic control, and fault diagnosis system.
The mechanical hydraulic system for the well wall masonry module uses single-cylinder hydraulic conveying and double-cylinder hydraulic conveying.
An independent hydraulic integration station, which avoids the impact of host vibration on the hydraulic system, ensuring the reliability of the hydraulic system.
The concrete culvert module brick-making equipment moves the feeding box and demolding box, closes the storage box door, and automatically transports the support board all independently by a hydraulic system, thus achieving reduced mechanical wear and maintenance.
The concrete inspection well module brick-making equipment uses imported computers, electrical components, seals, and hydraulic components to ensure the overall performance of the equipment is stable and reliable.
The mechanical shaker platform for the well wall masonry module uses a whole steel plate, with line cutting and mold assembly without welding points, allowing the filling box to swing freely for guidance, thus significantly reducing mechanical wear.
Reduce mold loading, compaction, and densification in one step with integrated, full-synchronous tangential and radial vibration to ensure compaction effectiveness.
Wall module of the well wall subjected to mechanical vibration by a mechanical shaker, with computer-automated control of amplitude that is adjusted according to raw material cost-effectiveness, without wear and tear brakes, thereby extending its service life and reducing costs.
The well wall masonry module has dual functionalities of automatic mechanical control and manual control.
