Chongqing vocational colleges pilot modern apprenticeship system; students are de facto employees of the enterprise upon enrollment - Xinhua News Agency
Yesterday, it was reported that this year, modern apprenticeship training models will be piloted in 60 vocational high schools in the city, with students participating in the pilot simultaneously holding the status of apprentices. After enrollment, these students will be preliminarily recruited as employees by the pilot enterprises.
The municipal education commission requires that enrollment procedures for vocational and technical schools and enterprise hiring programs be standardized, clarifying the dual identity of apprentice students at vocational and technical schools and prospective employees from enterprises. Apprentices, schools, and enterprises should sign a tripartite agreement based on the principle of mutual selection. For apprentices who are aged 16 or older but under 18 years old, a quadrilateral agreement must be signed among the apprentice, guardian, school, and enterprise to determine each party's rights and responsibilities, as well as specific job positions, teaching content, and rights protection during their on-the-job training.
Encourage pilot schools to adopt a modern apprenticeship model in collaboration with enterprises to conduct onboarding training and job-transition training for enterprise employees.
Pilot schools should reform their talent cultivation model.
Collaborate to design talent cultivation plans, jointly establish professional teaching standards, curriculum standards, job standards, standards for enterprise mentors, quality supervision standards, and corresponding implementation schemes.
The pilot program runs for an academic cycle designed to cultivate students, during which the duration of internships at enterprises is determined according to the professional talent training plan. Full-time internships generally last for six months.
Enterprise practice should implement an enterprise team-based management model, with each mentor taking on 2-5 apprentices based on their professional characteristics, forming learning groups to ensure that students master the skills required for each training position.
According to the plan, from 2016 to August 2019, the city determined three batches of 60 municipal secondary vocational modern apprenticeship pilot programs, with each program enrolling around 50 students (apprentices) in total, resulting in the cultivation of about 3,000 students (apprentices).
Following the principle of piloting first and then promoting, gradually advancing through points to areas, exploring and establishing a long-term mechanism for joint enrollment, joint cultivation, and integrated education between schools and enterprises, truly enhancing students' occupational skills, and improving their rate of matched employment and employment quality.
