The China Children's Center will host a series of activities to make "high-tech" the highlight of Children's Day - Xinhuanet.
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, May 20 (Huang Xiaoxi, Zhou Shanshan) It was learned from the China Children's Center on May 20 that during the period around Children's Day from June 28 to June 1, the center plans to hold a series of activities including children's maker experiences, a children's visual arts festival, and a parent-child reading carnival, allowing children to spend Children's Day immersed in the charm of cutting-edge technology.
According to reports, during this year's Children's Day in China, the activities organized by the Chinese Children's Center included the "Family Creativity" Children's Future Learning Carnival, the first Children's Visual Art Festival, the "Book Fair," and the "Family Love Reading" series of picture book activities.
Li Zhongming, deputy director of the China Children Center, introduced at a media briefing held on June 20th that the "Love Home Create Cool" Children's Future Learning Carnival is this year's key event organized by the China Children Center in celebration of Children's Day on June 1st.
The activities aim to fuse social innovation with individual family creativity by involving children and families in various innovative educational experiences, making innovation practice a cultural gene of mainstream families and "doing hands-on" a new learning and lifestyle for many families.
According to reports, "Love Home Create Cool" Children's Future Learning Carnival includes activities such as "Bean Curd Maker" experience, the anniversary celebration of Old Cow Children's Exploration Hall and the "Explore Family Love, Fun for Kids on Children's Day," VR Mass Experience Plan, and "Maker Tribe" interactive workshops, among others, featuring dozens of cutting-edge technology experiences.
