Wan teachers for rural primary schools in Jiangxi will be trained within three years – Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua News Agency, Nanchang, May 22 (Xinhua reporter Chen Yushan) Recently, the Jiujiang Provincial Education Department has informed that to enhance the capacity of teachers in key disciplines and achieve balanced development of primary education in rural areas, starting from 2016, Jiangxi plans to train 1,000 qualified music, art, and physical education teachers over three years for every primary school in the province's rural areas (townships and below).
It is understood that the target of this training includes other subject teachers in primary schools across rural areas of Jiangxi province who are under the age of 45 and have a foundational knowledge or talent in music, art, and physical education subjects, allowing them to teach these subjects alongside their main subjects.
Through training, they will acquire basic knowledge and teaching skills for subjects like music, physical education, and art, update their teaching ideas and concepts, master modern teaching methods, enhance their subject teaching abilities, activity design capabilities, campus culture abilities, and self-development capabilities, build a team of multi-skilled music, physical education, and art teachers, and alleviate the shortage of such teachers in rural areas.
To ensure quality and effectiveness of training, Jiangxi also plans to train one music, art, and physical education teacher in each of the province's 100 counties (cities, districts), totaling 300 trainers. These trainers will enhance their teaching demonstration and leading abilities, curriculum research activity design and organization skills, training capabilities, and network seminar workshop construction skills, serving as instructors, models, guides, and supervisors.
