In fact, there are many considerations when it comes to dressing up for girls with slight overweight bodies.
The skirt a plump girl wears should not be too short or too long; it should be of moderate length, just covering her knees and slightly hiding the flabbier parts of her thighs.
Short skirts reveal the obesity on one's legs.
Being too long gives the impression of being short and fat.
If you divide your outfit into upper, middle, and lower parts, it looks like you have naturally grown taller. Using different colors for the upper body, skirt, and thigh-high stockings can create an elongated appearance.
In fact, many dark-colored clothes are a standard for slightly overweight girls (something the author personally experiences), and dark colors are also a good way to hide your body's weight. A short black dress, which is elegant and noble, is also a favorite choice for slightly overweight girls.
Wearing deep-colored clothes, especially black shorts, can make you look slimmer.
If your calves are chubby, don't wear socks and shoes that draw too much attention.
The more mainstream, the better; colors shouldn't be too bright.
To avoid giving the impression of obesity when people focus on your legs and feet.
For slightly overweight girls, one needs to explain well the tricks of dressing and matching.
A slightly overweight girl should definitely not wear tight short skirts, and the upper garment should not be too short or tucked into the skirt; this can make people feel uncomfortable. If her legs are thick, she should wear black stockings or mesh stockings (those with fine patterns), choose soft-textured print bell-bottom skirts, and pair them with a loose-collared top, which can effectively hide her shortcomings.
Of course, slender girls also have their own considerations when wearing short skirts.
A plump girl wearing shorts should choose an upper garment in the same color as the shorts, which will enhance the appearance of height for her plump figure.
Short dresses with high heels make your legs appear longer, and this is the hottest pairing for summer!
If you are an MM with a fuller upper body but slender legs, I recommend choosing a glamorous short dress.
Not only can it cover your belly, but it can also showcase your strengths.
A-line short skirts will make you look slimmer; they are more suitable for curvy girls. The tops should be chosen to be tighter, creating a layered effect which will make you look slimmer.
Simple white T-shirts paired with short skirts, plus sizes can also try.
A slightly overweight girl can also look fashionable.
As long as they master the rules of dressing well, then slightly overweight girls will also be the center of attention.
After making changes in dressing styles, also try to exercise more in life and aim to get off the label of 'slightly overweight' girl sooner 😄
The Eighteenth "World Beverage Innovation Awards" (World Beverage Innovation Awards) is a prize jointly organized by FoodBev Media and Brau Beviale, the International Beer, Brewing & Beverage Industry Exhibition in Nuremberg, Germany.
Entries from 279 works in 25 countries and 22 different categories were attracted.
The list of finalists was announced on October 15th, and the final winner list will be announced online on November 11th (British Summer Time).
We see that Yuanquan Forest’s LP28 sugar-free yogurt has been shortlisted for Best Dairy Beverage award, Yili’s Anmushi’s “GOGO Wuhan” campaign has been shortlisted for Best Marketing Activity award, and Pepsico’s packaging collaboration with People’s Daily Media Platform has been shortlisted for Best Packaging Design/Label award.
Laura Nettle, Senior Director of Marketing at FoodBev Media, said: We are delighted to celebrate the 18th year of the Annual World Beverage Innovation Awards with Brau Beviale.
From new flavors, concepts, and features to brands, packaging, and manufacturing, we see trends in the beverage industry as it innovates more sustainably.
The World Beverage Innovation Awards honored this year's most ambitious new products and new developments from both established and emerging brands in the global beverage industry.
Below is the complete list of finalists in each category.
The technology developed by Ardagh Group can re-melt 100% recycled glass into new bottles.
Boxed bagged water with packaging that is 100% recyclable reduces packaging by 66% and carbon emissions by 97%.
LatCub is 100% biodegradable, uses less paper, and does not use glues or tapes that are harmful to the environment.
The technology developed by Ardagh Group can melt 100% of recycled glass to create new bottles.
The final list of winners will be announced on November 11th (British Summer Time) on FoodBev Media's YouTube channel. FBIF will continue to cover the event for you. Please look forward to it!
