What was the hottest thing in 2021?
Undoubtedly the Tokyo Olympics.
Do you think only Olympic athletes can win awards?
Recently, there was an article titled "Check this out! The Olympic Projects that Project Managers Can Reach Gold Medals For," which mentioned that project managers can absolutely lead in many projects without any competition: Moving bricks, traveling for work, and staying up late are part of the daily routine for project managers, while putting out fires, taking the blame, and apologizing are all common occurrences.
A seemingly light-hearted article reveals the daily hardships of project managers, and behind it lies a sense of inadequacy towards current project management work.
And personnel engaged in project management are also increasingly choosing actions to extricate themselves from the difficulties of their work.
With the increasing number of applicants for the PMP (Project Management Professional, an internationally recognized project management certification), more and more project management professionals are enhancing their project management capabilities through learning.
According to the "China's Twenty-Year Development Report on Project Management (1999-2019)", as of September 2019, the cumulative number of people who have taken the PMP® exam nationwide approached 600,000, with approximately 4.2 million people having obtained PMP® certification, and around 3 million people holding valid certificates, accounting for about 31.2% of the global pool of PMP® holders.
Over the past decade, the number of PMP holders has grown annually, indicating that project managers are increasingly aware that relying solely on past "old experience" to do things is no longer viable. The rapidly changing work environment teaches us that we must learn to explore and move forward by standing on the shoulders of scientific giants.
However, passing the PMP exam guarantees smooth sailing in project management work?
Many project management beginners state that by learning courses related to PMP/IPMP, they can systematically grasp the ten domains and five process groups of project management along with related knowledge points; however, when actually engaging in project management work, they still feel lost.
Many project managers often report the following issues: inadequate project management knowledge relying solely on personal experience, hollowed-out with project management theories, unable to put them into practice; lack of systematic project management processes and procedures, making it difficult to implement these processes in work, inaccurate project estimation, low responsiveness, and projects dragging on for too long; unclear member roles and responsibilities, baffled by how to deal with "seasoned veterans" within the team, poor cross-departmental collaboration leading to inefficient communication, making it hard to push the project forward…
Having focused on product innovation and research and development management for over a decade, we have helped numerous excellent enterprises cultivate a large number of product managers, project managers, and other key R&D talent, earning honors such as “Base for Training High-Quality Talent in China’s Enterprises for Research and Development Management.” With this in mind, Zhongtian Hexia Consulting brings you the Online Training Camp for Product Project Managers.
"Project Manager Training Camp" Online Course This is an online, fragmented learning approach that combines practical cases, tools, and methods from various R&D-oriented enterprises to help you master the essential knowledge and standardized steps for a project manager, leading you on the path to advancing your own project management skills.
This is also an opportunity for enterprises to promote the development of project managers at lower costs and with fewer resources, leading to efficient operations for the company.
Without a written record, you could first see how other students evaluate this course: Not only is it taught by an expert team from Zhong Tian Huaxia (originally Huawei's R&D management team), which integrates advanced project management methodologies from around the world with numerous real business scenarios of leading enterprises, but also provides in-depth and accessible professional explanations for its content.
It will also provide scientific and practical management tools and methods, as well as a wealth of templates and forms, to help participants apply what they have learned in their actual work after class.
