Before Double Twelve at Jetton, the company advocates rational consumption for consumers - Economic Observer - Professional Financial News Website
This year's "Singles' Day" carnival saw national online payment transaction amounts reach 1.77 trillion yuan, marking another record-high compared to previous years.
A variety of red packets with full-reduction offers, eye-catching live-streaming sales, once again have consumers exclaiming about their benefits. This wave of consumption not only makes one marvel at the growing consumer power of the nation, but also forces one to cool down and think about the impact of consumerism on society and the contemporary mainstream consumer group.
Prior to Double Twelve, Leijinqing Consumer Finance Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as “Leijinqing”) issued a call for rational consumption, reminding its users, particularly young people, to foster good consumption awareness and habits and to refuse blind and excessive consumption.
According to the Consumer Finance Literacy Survey Analysis Report released this year by the People's Bank of China, the national consumer finance literacy index is 66.81, up 2.04 from 2019.
Overall, Chinese residents perform well in financial consumption, but exhibit significant differences in various aspects of financial behavior and skills, and need to further improve their foundational knowledge of finance.
The level of financial literacy among the elderly and adolescents is relatively low, and the elderly and young people will continue to be the focus of ongoing attention in financial education; the Young China Youth Liability Report published by Nielsen and the Young China Youth Consumption Report 2019-2020 published by Central Finance showed that the young generation has a huge consumption potential, and credit consumption has become an important way of increasing consumption. 86.6% of young people are using credit products, almost half of whom have no debt accumulation.
As a licensed consumer finance institution, JiXin has been dedicated to providing high-quality, considerate services to help citizens build their own happy lives. It promotes consumers to establish good and correct consumption concepts and actively responds to regulatory calls to raise rational consumption awareness among consumers, especially young groups, through practical actions.
Over the past several years, Credence has conducted comprehensive and diverse financial literacy campaigns targeting young groups such as college students, and has guided their consumption demands in a reasonable manner through various forms, including innovation practice competitions with top domestic universities, to help them establish rational consumption concepts, plan their needs reasonably, and assist them in accumulating wealth for their lives.
Ahead of Double Twelve, Zhixin reminds all consumers to develop reasonable consumption awareness and a proper perspective on money, resist blind and excessive spending, avoid misconceptions about consumption loans, and prevent it from affecting personal credit as well as future economic life.
One must plan ahead and stay within one's means when spending and make timely repayments.
If it is overdue, a late payment record will be added to your personal credit report, which may have negative impacts on future economic activities such as buying a car or a house.
Meanwhile, when enjoying financial products and services, one should choose legitimate institutions and channels and verify whether the relevant institutions have the necessary operating licenses.
In the future, CreditEase will continue to provide consumers with more tailored and diversified services through its mature and reliable consumer finance system and constantly updated financial products, helping to enhance public financial literacy. It will also help consumers develop the mindset of rational consumption and moderate borrowing, serving as a trusted consumer finance partner for life.
