Syncing the University Spirit with the Spirit of the Age - Xinhua News Agency
The spirit of a university refers to a set of educational philosophies and value pursuits that have been long-accumulated over the course of its development, constituting the soul of the university.
Throughout history, the spirit of the university has been crucial for the development of politics, economy, culture, science and technology, society, and even a nation's progress.
From the birth of the first modern university as we know it, universities have borne a unique mission distinct from other organizations. For our universities, which emerged during a time of national peril, this spirit has been deeply influenced by traditional culture and the evolution of times. They advocate values such as "morality for the benefit of the world, rectification of self and peace throughout the state," and the patriotic duty of "promoting learning to strengthen the nation."
Currently, there is an increasingly evident trend of informatization and internationalization in higher education, with intensified global competition in education, science and technology, and talent. As an important "supply-side" sector, the structural reform of higher education is facing unprecedented opportunities and challenges.
The especially the proposal of the “Overall Plan for the Comprehensive Promotion of World-Class University and Disciplinary Construction,” which not only demonstrates China’s confidence and determination to move from a major country in higher education to a strong country in higher education, but also sets higher and more updated requirements for university development.
How can we quickly strive to enter the ranks of world-class players while still having some distance to cover, and accelerate the construction of several world-class universities and a number of world-class disciplines, in order to achieve “leapfrogging” development?
Besides being confident in their goals, path, and capabilities, universities should also leverage three key strengths: first, the advantage of being a latecomer, through continuous recruitment of distinguished overseas academic talents and learning from the best practices of world-class universities to significantly enhance academic standards and institutional quality; second, cultural advantage, by inheriting the wisdom embedded in five millennia of Chinese civilization and promoting and developing excellent traditional culture in order to rally forces, brand themselves, and elevate their image; and third, institutional advantage, by tapping into the superior institutional advantages of a socialist country, driving toward objectives, consolidating shared consensus, optimizing resource allocation, and providing a robust sustainable foundation for the schools to accelerate catching up with world-leading standards.
It is particularly important to realize that building world-class universities cannot be one-size-fits-all, and each school must highlight its own strengths while showcasing its unique character and characteristics.
The characteristics of education must have both commonalities with Chinese characteristics and reflect their unique goals, institutional traditions, and resource endowments.
For Zhejiang University, we focus on three distinctive features in our operations: first, emphasizing the cultivation of entrepreneurial and innovative talent, building an integrated education environment that combines education and science and technology with industry and enterprises to form a complete entrepreneurial education ecosystem; second, emphasizing the convergence of disciplines, driving the optimization and adjustment of the disciplinary system, fostering an institutional environment for interdisciplinary work, and actively nurturing emerging interdisciplinary disciplines and landmark interdisciplinary achievements; third, focusing on the educational system and social service features, deepening international cooperation, and accelerating the formation of a broader partnership network for research, education, and innovation around Zhejiang University.
During this process, it is especially important to uphold university spirit and ensure that it resonates with the spirit of the times.
For Zhejiang University, the motto "Innovation for the Quest for Truth," the shared values of "study diligently, cultivate morality, discern clearly, and practice earnestly," along with the shared spirit encapsulated in "Encompassing rivers and seas, enlightening truth, nurturing virtue, and benefiting the people, building our nation," constitute the latest expression system of Zhejiang University's spirit.
This is an essential safeguard for the school to uphold its correct educational mission and continuously accumulate cultural heights and spiritual strength; it is rich in content and of profound significance.
Among them, "Oceanic and Riverine" stresses an open and inclusive spirit, reflecting a mindset of harnessing the talents of the world, manifested in absorbing the best educational philosophies from world-renowned institutions; "Awakening Truth and Cultivating Virtue" emphasizes a spirit of seeking truth and goodness, which means that universities should not only pursue truth but also be nourished by moral cultivation and shaped by personal development; "Opening Up the World and Benefiting the People" embodies a spirit of innovation and reform, encompassing both the pursuit of new knowledge and innovative research, as well as reform and renewal; "Raising Our Homeland" stresses a patriotic dedication spirit, which means that universities should always stand shoulder to shoulder with the fate of the nation.
These set of spiritual principles and value pursuits is precisely what has been at the soul of Zhejiang University’s 120 years of establishment.
"Smart ears hear without sound, wise eyes see before things take shape."
China’s universities should further position themselves within the broader context of socialism with Chinese characteristics, deeply understanding their era’s place and historical mission in the higher education sector, and accelerate efforts to build world-class universities.
At the same time, upholding humanistic care and independent freedom allows university spirit to resonate with the spirit of the times and the national spirit, thus providing inexhaustible motivation for achieving national prosperity and the rejuvenation of the nation, as well as realizing humanity’s common ideals.
