Iranian President: Nuclear negotiations with Iran could succeed if sanctions are lifted - Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua News Agency, Tehran, December 11 (Xinhua reporters Gao Wencheng and Wang Shoubao) President of Iran Ebrahim Raisi said on Thursday that if the US lifts sanctions against Iran, negotiations on the comprehensive Iran nuclear deal can reach a "good agreement."
According to a message released on Iran's President’s website, Ali Khamenei said during a meeting with Iranian ambassadors to neighboring countries that Iran has shown its negotiating good faith by submitting proposals to other parties to the nuclear agreement.
If the US is determined, “the path to an agreement will be smooth.”
Related parties to the Iran nuclear agreement began talks in Vienna, the capital of Austria, this April to discuss the resumption of compliance by the US and Iran.
Round 1 negotiations began on November 29 in Vienna and were temporarily adjourned on December 3 to reconvene on December 9.
