Xi Jinping sends congratulatory message to the 2021 Greater Bay Area Science Forum - Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua Beijing, December 11 – President Xi Jinping of the People's Republic of China sent a message of congratulations to the 2021 Greater Bay Area Science Forum on December 11.
Xi pointed out that the world is currently undergoing a major transformation of historic proportions, with global science and technology innovation entering a period of high activity, and new rounds of technological revolution and industrial transformation having a profound impact on the global economic structure.
The Greater Bay Area of Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao should focus on its strategic positioning as an international center for innovation and technology, work to build a global hub for innovation, and drive the development of emerging industries.
China is willing to work with scientists from all over the world and international scientific organizations to enhance international cooperation and exchanges in science and technology, strengthen research on major scientific issues, promote breakthroughs in common technologies, deepen collaboration on key scientific projects, and jointly advance the development of global scientific progress for the greater benefit of mankind.
The 2021 Greater Bay Area Science Forum opened on Monday in Guangzhou, Guangdong Province, with the theme of "Exploring the Future, Sharing Science," and was hosted by the Government of Guangdong Province.
