As NFTs were rapidly gaining traction, another new concept emerged in the crypto community.
In 2021, a blockchain game called Axie Infinity had a significant impact in Southeast Asia, where some residents, who lost job opportunities due to the pandemic, began earning stable income from playing the game.
Axie Infinity is a blockchain-based pet-raising game that brings together a variety of toys, including NFTs, and is currently the highest-grossing NFT project with over $3 billion in transactions to date.
TokenTerminal data shows that Axie Infinity daily revenue exceeds $8.2 million, nearing that of Honor of Kings.
On August 6th this year, Axie Infinity officially announced that its daily active users exceeded 1 million.
The popularity of "Axie Infinity" has spread a new "play-to-earn" model, where blockchain and smart contracts help players no longer remain single roles. Beyond gaining enjoyment and economic benefits from the game, they can also participate in the governance of the game's ecosystem.
This subjectivity is not granted by the game developers but ensured by blockchain technology.
When I saw the news about friends' share prices, I was most touched by the choice of companies on the racetrack, i.e. the choice of industries to invest in, first to choose a large growth space with a market size of at least 100 billion; second, to choose an industry that will grow well in the future, considering the best state of industry growth in the next 3-5 years; and finally, to choose an industry that has policy support.
The width of the track refers to the size of the market, the length of the track refers to the development phase of the industry, and the flatness or roughness of the track refers to the competitive landscape of the industry.
For the right track!
The first thing in this new year is to summarize 2021 and adjust the tactical layout for 2022.
The tactic lies in "doing things right," that is, getting things right.
And the strategy lies in “doing the right thing,” which means doing the right thing.
Strategy lies in finding direction, and tactics lie in implementation. There is room for strategic thinking above most tactical considerations.
For instance, instead of focusing on increasing customer numbers (tactical thinking), one can think about either deepening within the current domain or expanding horizontally to adjacent domains (strategic thinking); for example, instead of improving customer retention rates (tactical thinking), one can focus on boosting the retention rates of core customers and high-value customers (strategic thinking); atop enhancing activity participation rates (tactical thinking), one can consider how to set correct KPIs for activities, achieving the right goals such as boosting target customer participation, activating high-value dormant customers, and targeting new users accurately; atop boosting DAU (tactical thinking), one can assess whether current growth is healthy and sustainable.
Bitcoin, which has been in existence for twelve years, reached several milestone events in 2021.
On September 7, the small Central American country of El Salvador made Bitcoin its legal currency, making Bitcoin the first to become a legally sanctioned currency of a country or region.
On October 12, the US Securities and Exchange Commission approved ProShares' launch of a Bitcoin ETF for the first time in eight years, and listed it on the New York Stock Exchange. This marks the debut of a compliant Bitcoin futures ETF on the US capital market, expanding the crypto-currency investment exposure.
From the perspective of the development of blockchain technology, Bitcoin is not the star.
On November 14, 2021, Bitcoin underwent a soft fork upgrade called "Taproot," which increased the anonymity of transactions on the Bitcoin network and reduced the data burden in transactions by altering the data structure within blocks.
