Do you encounter any issues with continuing education hours for first-level cost engineer initial registration?
Persons who register late have not provided proof of continuing education. Persons who register late should provide proof of continuing education with at least 30 credits in the past year. Persons who re-register should provide proof of continuing education with at least 120 credits over the past four years. Persons who re-register should provide proof of continuing education learning with at least 30 credits for every full year.
Standard Continuing Education Fees for Cost Engineers
Cost engineers participating in online continuing education must pay a learning fee to their respective management bodies when registering. Generally, the standard cost is as follows: the fee for 30 compulsory hours of study is 300 yuan per person per year (including the unified textbooks for continuing education).
The fee for an elective course of 30 hours is 300 yuan per person per year.
The fee for the required 30-credit course and the elective 30-credit course is 600 yuan/person/year (inclusive of the unified textbook for continuing education).
Participation in online continuing education for registered cost engineers organized by CPCA or provincial and departmental management institutions will be credited based on the recorded time of online learning courses.
(B) Attending concentrated face-to-face training and various types of training sessions and seminars organized by the CPCA or provincial and departmental management institutions can each be recognized as four academic credits per half day.
Participation in continuing education lectures organized by CPCA, provincial and departmental cost engineers and cost estimators will be recognized as 10 academic credits per half day.
(IV) Participating in China Price Association and provincial research projects, industry standards compilation, and textbook writing is recognized as 30 academic credits per year for each project.
(Six) Participating in the compilation of textbooks for the National Engineering Cost Engineer's Qualification Examination, as well as in the creation of questions, review of questions, and grading, can earn 30 credits per year.
(A) Papers and books related to engineering valuation authored under a personal name and publicly published (as per official serial numbers).
Publishing a book of 10,000 words is recognized as 12 credits.
Publishing a paper in a national journal is recognized as 8 credits per thousand words, publishing a paper in a provincial journal is recognized as 5 credits per thousand words, and publishing a paper in a municipal journal is recognized as 3 credits per thousand words.
(Ninth) Attending open training organized by engineering cost consulting firms approved or authorized by the China Cost Association, provincial and departmental management institutions, and provincial cost associations (excluding general enterprise management and skills training), earns 4 credits per half day, with a maximum of 30 credits per year.
Procurement Engineer Network Continuing Education Learning Process
Upon registration fees being received by the registration institution, the learner’s identity is then activated, allowing the registered Cost Engineer to log in with their username and password to access the network education classroom.
Students learn through on-demand courseware, asking and answering questions, and online discussions.
If you forget your password and are unable to log in due to incorrect username and password when trying to access your course materials, please contact your registration agency, which can assist in changing your password (but not your username), allowing you to log in with the updated password.
