Education News: Beijing Reduces Proportion of Special Talent Admissions for Middle School Entrance in 2016 - Xinhua Net
On the two days of January 21st and 22nd, the Beijing Municipal Education Commission organized and implemented the examination for talented students in junior high school admissions through each district's education commission.
This year, the enrollment ratio of specialized students has been reduced in every district in Beijing, making competition for these students more intense.
For example, in Dongcheng District, this year the overall percentage of elementary school students admitted to junior high schools through special talent programs does not exceed 5% of the district's enrollment plan, with an enrollment plan of 380 students; the admission rate to schools does not exceed 10% of the school’s enrollment plan.
All students who have a special education in sports, arts and technology and are enrolled online are eligible to take the special education entrance exam.
To facilitate students in attending inspections conveniently nearby, Dongcheng District will continue the inspection arrangement from last year, setting 1-2 inspection sites in each study zone, totaling 13 inspection sites.
The examination will be conducted within the different examination districts on the day of the examination.
On May 23, the list of students who passed the examination was publicly displayed on the district education and recruitment examination center's website, and students could check their examination results online.
