48 Hours of Nuclear Acid Negative, Buffer Zone Establishment of the Joint State Council Joint Defense Control Mechanism to Strengthen Coastal City Epidemic Control - Xinhua Network
Xinhua Beijing, December 11 (Ding Ruofeng and Gu Tiancheng) -- The State Council Joint Prevention and Control Mechanism recently issued an instruction on strengthening COVID-19 prevention and control in border cities. It requires that people who recently left land-border port cities (excluding those connected to Hong Kong and Macau) need to present a negative nucleic acid test within 48 hours, while those who travel to border port cities should undergo at least one nucleic acid test upon arrival.
According to the notification, the time frame for the above requirements is from the day on which the provincial regions and municipalities determine the scope of border cities and announce it, until March 15, 2022.
Furthermore, the notice also proposes that cities with ports of entry may study establishing buffer zones for epidemic prevention and control within their jurisdictions.
A relevant official from the National Health Commission's Department of Disease Prevention and Control introduced that for some border cities, cross-border border trade is a major economic pillar, with frequent interactions between both sides' residents.
Implementing differentiated management policies for different areas transforms one barrier to contain external spread into two barriers, potentially shifting the focus of control towards earlier stages and compressing the risk of regional transmission. This approach aims to achieve the greatest public health outcome with the least social impact and cost in epidemic control.
Recently, multiple local cluster outbreaks in China have occurred, all of which are due to imported cases from border cities abroad.
The announcement noted that this exposed problems such as inadequate early warning of local surveillance of epidemics, non-implementation of close-loop management of high-risk positions, regular detection of nucleic acid flows into the form, non-destruction of cold chain items, non-regulation of the management of concentrated quarantine facilities, insufficient scientific accuracy of emergency management of epidemics, etc.
The notice requires focusing on nine aspects, including improving epidemic prevention mechanisms in border cities, strengthening pandemic monitoring and early warning systems, and implementing border control measures, to accelerate the rectification of weaknesses and shortcomings in port city defenses. It calls for unwavering, precise, and scientific efforts in prevention and control work to tighten and reinforce the defense against external input.
The notice emphasizes that port cities should concurrently study and deploy measures for epidemic prevention and control with their work on ensuring public welfare, and should publish and ensure smooth flow of hotline services for public welfare. They should periodically identify early signs of issues related to the supply and price of basic living necessities, and promptly address and actively respond to public concerns about prominent problems.
According to the notification, the port cities referred to include counties (cities, districts, or banners) and the cities (regions, prefectures, or leagues) where open land, water, and air ports are located, as well as their respective direct-controlled municipalities. The specific scope will be determined based on epidemic prevention needs by each provincial (autonomous region, municipality directly under the central government) and announced in a timely manner.
