Sino-Saudi curators collaborate to host Saudi Arabia's first contemporary art biennial - Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua Riyadh, December 12 – (By Wang Haizhou and Hu Guan) The first Contemporary Art Biennial in Saudi Arabia, Diriyah Contemporary Art Biennial, officially opened to the public on November 1st at the JAX Art District in Diriyah, located northwest of Saudi capital Riyadh. Featuring works by 64 artists from Saudi Arabia and other parts of the world, the exhibition has started.
This biennial exhibition is co-curated by the Diyar Biennial Foundation of Saudi Arabia and UCCA Center for Contemporary Art in China, with director Tian Fei-yu serving as the artistic director.
According to the curatorial team, the theme of this biennial exhibition is "Crossing the river by feeling for stones," which metaphorically refers to the reform strategies adopted during periods of social and economic transition, and also reflects the current situation of Saudi society and culture.
This biennial exhibition covers nearly 12,000 square meters and spans six interconnected buildings, presenting six units: “Crossing the River by Feeling for Stones,” “Tradition as Experiment,” “Thinking at the Margin,” “Engaging the Public,” “A Beautiful New World,” and “On the Spirit of Art.”
Among them, the number of works by 27 Saudi artists accounts for more than four-fifths of the total exhibition, covering various forms such as painting, installation art, and performance art; twelve Chinese artists' works also garnered significant attention, with some using recycled materials in innovative ways, such as Cai Guoqiang who, in his work "The Series Behind the Story - The Unfathomable Mountain Stream Landscape" (2014), re-constructed a classic landscape painting using waste materials.
Chief Executive of the Dijlah Biennial Foundation, Buckley, said that he hoped this edition of the biennial would establish an international dialogue, giving global audiences the opportunity to understand Saudi Arabia's burgeoning cultural and creative industries and communities, and fostering greater interactions.
Tian Feiyu said: "The goal of the biennial is two-fold: to involve contemporary Saudi art in global conversations and to enable Saudi audiences to engage with the world of contemporary art."
It is reported that during the run-up to the biennial exhibition, there will also be a series of lectures where artists, curators, and leaders in the creative industry will discuss topics such as cross-cultural exchange and the development of contemporary art.
