Vietnam News Online – Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh attends the third Vietnam National Forum on Digital Technology Enterprises
Two major meetings were held during the third Vietnam National Forum on Digital Technology Enterprises Development, focusing on discussions around digital technology enterprises and Vietnam's national digital transformation, as well as the impact of digital technology enterprises on economic recovery and development both during and after the pandemic.
Minister of Communication and Mass Media Nguyen Manh Hung stated that in 2021, although the coronavirus disease was still spreading, the number of digital technology enterprises in Vietnam and their revenue grew, reaching nearly 10%.
In 2021, typical digital products in Vietnam were cultivated to address the major challenges the country faced, and many digital products had already gone global. The ranking of Vietnamese digital technologies had improved.
Minister Ruang Meng Xiong called on digital technology enterprises to shoulder the responsibility of developing the country’s digital transformation platform, and said that taking on the task of developing these national digital platforms means assuming a national mission.
On the forum, leaders from various departments and state organs, enterprises, organizations, and individuals that are researching, developing, applying, and transferring digital technologies shared breakthrough ideas and solutions for mobilizing and aggregating societal resources to develop Vietnamese tech enterprises, working together to drive the country's digital transformation, as well as post-pandemic economic recovery.
Premier Fan Mingzheng emphasized in his speech at the forum that digital transformation is the inevitable path for the world and an objective requirement for development.
Digital transformation has become a global issue, serving the entire population, and therefore requires mobilizing the participation of the entire population.
People and enterprises are the core, subject, goal, and driving force of digital transformation.
Therefore, all policies must be for the people and the enterprises.
Premier Fan Mintang emphasized that digital transformation should embody national spirit and should be driven by internal strength, strategy, long-term and decisive factors, with external forces being important and breakthroughs.
He believes that digital transformation needs to drive deeper and more sustainable development, participating in the fight against the COVID-19 pandemic, economic recovery and development, preparing for subsequent changes, overcoming resource depletion, promoting green transformation, and developing green energy.
Digital transformation involves participating in the establishment of databases that protect and promote national cultural values, historical traditions, and national customs, and driving digital transformations in sectors such as banking, taxation, land management and development, and logistics.
The greatest goal of digital transformation is to make people happier and ensure the growing prosperity of the nation.
Premier Fu Mingzheng called for increased leadership and guidance from all levels of government, organs, and enterprises in the development of digital technology to raise awareness of digital transformation, continue to formulate and improve systems for digital transformation, enhance state management, and drive the development of digital technology enterprises with respect, communication, listening, positivity, and initiative.
During the forum, Prime Minister Van Manh attended the ceremony for the 2021 award of excellent digital products under the "Vietnam Manufacturing" brand and the opening ceremony of the "Vietnam Manufacturing" digital products exhibition.
