"Smart Integration of Xiangyang" 2021 China International Rail Transit and Equipment Manufacturing Industry Talent Summit Opens - Rolling News - Hunan Daily Network - Huanxiang Online
The Hunan Daily reports (Xuzhihan, Full-Media Reporter) that on the 10th, the “Smart Gathering Xiangxiang” 2021 International High-Speed Rail and Equipment Manufacturing Industry Human Talent Summit opened in Zhuzhou.
Wang Cheng, member of the Standing Committee of the Provincial Party Committee and Minister of the Provincial Organization Department, attended the launch ceremony and delivered a speech.
Wang Cheng pointed out that hosting a talent summit is an important measure to implement the spirit of the Central Conference on Talent Work and the 12th Party Congress of the Province, showcasing Hunan's genuine commitment to valuing, seeking out, and utilizing talent.
Hunan has a fine tradition of valuing talent, respecting talent, and nurturing talent, as well as broad platforms for developing talent and favorable conditions for achieving a better life. In recent years, it has deeply implemented a strategy to lead development through talent, with the Fenghuo Talent Action Plan serving as a driving force. This has established a comprehensive talent work pattern that covers recruitment, cultivation, retention, and utilization. As a result, it has become a fertile ground for talent growth and achievement, a hotbed for innovation and entrepreneurship, and a desirable place to live and work.
Currently, Hunan is fully implementing the strategic positioning and mission of “Three Highs and Four New Things,” and will further open doors for attracting talents and fostering entrepreneurship, offering better policies, concentrating more resources, and creating better conditions to support talent innovation and entrepreneurship. It looks forward to outstanding talents from all sectors coming together to pool their wisdom and efforts for high-quality development in Hunan.
The exhibition featured pavilions for Changsha, Zhuzhou, and Xiangtan, as well as a booth for Hunan Free Trade Zone. The Provincial Department of Science and Technology, Provincial Department of Industry and Information Technology, and Provincial Department of Human Resources and Social Security released a list of key innovation and technological needs in advanced manufacturing-related industries, a directory of talent requirements in the smart manufacturing industry, and a directory of young talents' demand for intelligent manufacturing at postdoctoral flow stations.
48 large enterprises such as China Railway Rolling Stock Corporation, Zhonglun Heavy Industry, and Fargrand Technology conducted on-site recruitment, with over a thousand relevant professional graduates and social talents participating in talent matching projects.
