The Yangtze River main stem achieves full coverage of waterborne green comprehensive service areas - Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua Wuhan, Dec 11 (Xinhua reporter Wang Xian) The Wulong waterborne integrated service area for green development in Chongqing was completed and put into operation on Sunday, the second such service area for green water transport services officially operating downstream of the Yangtze River after the Liulong area in Sichuan Province was inaugurated on Saturday.
So far, the water-green integrated service area has covered the upper, middle and lower reaches of the Yangtze River.
Qiu Jianhua, Deputy Director of the Yangtze Navigation Administration under the Ministry of Transport, introduced that so far, ten green comprehensive service areas for waterborne transport have been built and put into operation in the middle and lower reaches of the Yangtze River in provinces such as Hubei, Hunan, Jiangxi, Anhui, and Jiangsu, which have received widespread recognition from crew members and played an important role in promoting the high-quality development of Yangtze River shipping.
The full coverage of green integrated service areas on water is another milestone in the construction of green shipping on the Yangtze River, significantly enhancing the reception and handling capacity of ship pollutants on the Yangtze River.
According to the introduction, the green integrated service area on water is an important facility that provides comprehensive production and living services for ships and seafarers, helping to address the "urgent, difficult, and concerning" issues faced by seafarers.
The two newly built and operational green comprehensive service areas on the Yangtze River's upper reaches integrate living services, production services, and government services under one roof, with a theme focused on green and environmental protection. The areas specialize in ship maintenance and emergency rescue services, aiming to enable ships in port to receive "multiple services in one berthing," which will make it more efficient for crew members who undertake year-round navigation on the Yangtze River, and their lives more convenient.
US deploys three aircraft carriers near China; US Navy's most powerful weapon makes rare visit to Guam, sending important signals to America's allies and adversaries in the Indo-Pacific region.
According to the China think tank "Nanhai Strategic Situation Awareness Platform," on January 9th, a satellite detected the USS Carl Vinson aircraft carrier of the US Navy in the Bashi Channel vicinity.
The Baracoa Strait connects the South China Sea and Sulu Sea and is a strategic location in the First Island Chain of the Western Pacific.
The platform expects that the USS Carl Vinson will deploy to the South China Sea.
This is the first deployment of the aircraft carrier USS Carl Vinson to carry F-35C fighter jets and CMV-22 "Osprey" deck-based transport aircraft.
Currently sailing in the Pacific are US Navy aircraft carriers other than the USS Carl Vinson, which set sail from the United States on January 3rd with the USS Abraham Lincoln.
The USS "Lincoln" also carried an F-35C carrier squadron for the first time, which is part of the Marine Corps' 314th Fighter Attack Wing.
In addition to the two aircraft carriers mentioned above, currently deployed in the Asia-Pacific region by the US Navy is the aircraft carrier USS Ronald Reagan, which is berthed in Yokosuka, Japan.
Included in the Carrier Battle Group are the guided-missile cruiser Lake Superior and the guided-missile destroyer Sterkeveld.
U.S.S. carriers are gathering around China, the most powerful weapon rarely visits Guam on January 17, 2022, the Yangtze Strategic Positioning Platform released the latest satellite images showing three U.S.S. carriers are gathering around China.
U.S. carriers are gathering the most powerful weapons around China to reach Guam on January 17, 2022, the U.S. Navy's shipping carrier CMV-22B flight route.
(CNN, Weibo @SouthChinaSeaStrategicSituationalAwareness) According to a report by CNN on January 17, one of the US Navy's most powerful weapons visited Guam last weekend, an unusual occurrence.
The USS Nevada (a Ohio-class nuclear submarine carrying 20 Trident ballistic missiles and dozens of nuclear warheads) entered the US Naval Base in Guam last Saturday (January 15th).
Three US aircraft carriers gather near China's periphery; its most powerful weapon visits Guam for a rare occasion. Analysis says this is sending a signal to allies and adversaries in the region as tensions in the Indian-Pacific area rise.
This is the first visit to Guam by an American ballistic missile submarine since 2016 and the second public visit to Guam since the 1980s.
Three U.S. aircraft carriers gather near China's periphery, and its most powerful weapon visits Guam for a rare occasion. China has been constructing a large number of military facilities in the Spratly Islands in recent years.
Image of Yongshu Reef in the Paracel Islands belonging to China.
(The South China Sea Research Forum) The U.S. Navy stated in its declaration that the visit to Guam by the Ohio-class submarine USS Nevada enhanced cooperation between the United States and its regional allies, showcased the capabilities, flexibility, and readiness of the U.S., as well as its ongoing commitment to the security and stability of the Indo-Pacific region.
Ballistic missile submarines are typically referred to as "boomers" (Boomer submarine).
The whereabouts of 14 "Reaper submarines" in the U.S. Navy fleet are typically tightly classified.
The secrecy surrounding ballistic missile submarines makes them "the most important survivable weapon" in the "nuclear triad," which also includes land-based intercontinental ballistic missiles in the United States, as well as B-2 and B-52 bombers that can carry nuclear warheads.
Talking to friends about Meta's recent drop of 26%, losing $251 billion in market value, Zuckerberg responded with "facing unprecedented competition." Why was this the case?
Meta (formerly Facebook) is essentially an ad company, primarily generating revenue from ads, and today's ad companies that make money have their own traffic channels.
Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp, etc., are all traffic channels for Meta regardless of their function.
Moreover, Meta is also the largest "ad network," with many apps connecting their ads to Meta's platform for monetization.
But times have changed.
First, due to Apple's privacy policy changes, Meta has found it difficult to obtain user data, which impacts the efficiency of its advertising campaigns.
Apple's current privacy policy is user-friendly and clearly prompts users whether to allow an app to access their information. Most people’s normal reaction would be to refuse.
Next, if Google cuts off Meta again, the impact on Meta's revenue would be even greater.
Second, the China factor in Meta’s revenue growth has weakened (the weight of this factor is uncertain but it does exist).
Everyone knows that Meta does not have operations in China, but this understanding is not accurate.
Meta earns at least 10% of its revenue annually from China, mainly contributed by companies that have gone global from China.
Meta's office in Hong Kong has around several hundred people, and there are several major agents in mainland China.
Chinese companies want to expand into overseas markets, and Meta is an advertising channel they cannot avoid spending money on, with most of their spending going to Meta.
Interestingly, Toutiao is now one of ByteDance's main competitors for Meta, but Meta made quite a bit of money from ByteDance in the past two years.
All domestic agents are helping ByteDance advertise with Meta, and Meta's performance in Greater China is also doing well.
I haven't specifically gone to learn about it recently, but it certainly won't be better than before.
The phase of large-scale spending by Chinese companies overseas is over.
Third, new traffic channels have not been expanded smoothly.
Facebook is getting older, with new platforms like TT not in Meta's hands.
The biggest problem is not just a decline in income but a lack of growth expectations.
The capital market looks not just at current income but more importantly at what the future expectations are.
Clearly, Meta's expectations are insufficient.
To tell new stories to the market, Zuckerberg talked about the "metaverse."
The Metaverse should indeed be one of the future directions, but the timeline to realize the Metaverse is long, and this story may not be sufficient to justify Meta's current market valuation over the next couple of years.
So the next two years should be a difficult period for Meta.
Despite Facebook now being very prosperous, it brings in anywhere from $100 billion to $200 billion in annual revenue, it actually feels very threatened. Compared to other internet companies and technology firms, it has no good safe moat.
Although his several social apps have high daily active users and are mainstream social platforms like Facebook and WhatsApp, Facebook lacks confidence in the rapid development of TikTok. Disruption can happen in an instant.
While the concept of the Metaverse, which is out of reach in the short term and therefore has no hope of success, makes Facebook extremely dangerous, which is why Zuckerberg keeps changing his company’s name and constantly searching for new opportunities. However, I believe that the path he chose is wrong and leads to a dead end. These are some of my thoughts for reference.
Section 17: The state implements a registration management system for registered fire engineers.
Persons holding qualifications for Registered Fire Engineer at Level I or Level II shall practice under the name of the corresponding level Registered Fire Engineer after registration.
Eighteen. The Registration Approval Department for First-Class Registered Fire Engineers is the Fire Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security.
The provincial, autonomous region, and municipal public security fire protection bureaus are the departments responsible for registering second-level registered fire engineers, and they also undertake the preliminary review of applications for first-level registered fire engineers.
Article 19: A person who obtains a first-level or second-level registered fire engineer’s certificate and applies for registration shall be employed by a fire technology service institution that has been approved or a key unit in terms of fire safety, and shall submit the application materials through the public security fire institution of the unit where he/she is employed (if the employing unit is an enterprise, through the enterprise to the public security fire institution of its place of business registration).
Twenty: Within five working days of receiving an applicant's registration application, the public security fire department of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the central government shall inform the applicant in writing, if the materials submitted are incomplete or do not conform to legal form, of all the content that needs to be corrected; failure to provide such notice within the stipulated time will be deemed as acceptance from the date the application materials were received.
For registration applications that are accepted or not accepted, a written voucher shall be issued bearing the dedicated seal of the public security fire institution at this level and noting the date.
Twenty-first: The public security fire department of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall complete the preliminary review of the application materials for first-class registered fire engineer qualifications and the registration approval for second-class registered fire engineers within 20 working days after accepting the application, according to the prescribed conditions and procedures. It shall then submit the application materials for first-class registered fire engineer qualifications and the preliminary review opinion to the Public Security Fire Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security for approval.
The Ministry of Public Security's Fire Bureau shall make a decision on whether to approve within 20 working days from the date of receiving the application materials submitted by the provincial public security fire institutions and their preliminary review opinions.
Where an approval decision cannot be made within the prescribed period, the extension of the period and the reasons for such extension shall be notified to the applicant.
For decisions not to approve, reasons should be provided in writing, and the applicant should be informed of the right to apply for administrative review or bring an administrative lawsuit according to law.
The department responsible for approving registration shall issue and deliver the corresponding level of registration certificate within ten working days of making its approval decision.
The validity period of each registration certificate is 3 years.
The registration certificate is the practice credential for a registered fire engineer of a certain level valid within its validity period, and it shall be kept and used by the registered fire engineer himself/herself.
Article 24: Initial registration shall be applied for within one year from the date of obtaining the first or second-level registered fire engineer qualification certificate.
To apply for initial registration upon overdue, one must meet the continuing education requirements stipulated in this regulation.
Specific procedures for initial registration, continuation of registration, changes to registration, cancellation of registration, and non-registration will be regulated by the Ministry of Public Security separately.
Continued education is a mandatory condition for continuing registration, re-registration, and delayed initial registration of registered fire engineers.
During each valid registration period, registered fire engineers at all levels shall complete the corresponding continuing education as required.
Article 26 The department responsible for reviewing and approving registration shall promptly make public information regarding the registration of fire engineers, establish an archive on the professional conduct of registered fire engineers, and implement credit management of their practice activities.
Article 27: The registration management departments for registered fire engineers at all levels shall strictly enforce the provisions of the Administrative Licensing Law of the People's Republic of China.
This is the end of today's sharing on exam information; I hope it can be of some help to you.
Everyone must work hard to prepare and strive to pass the fire engineer exam as soon as possible!
