The joint medical exercise "Peace Rescue 2021" between Chinese and Vietnamese armed forces concludes successfully - Xinhua News Agency
On the morning of December 12, the Chinese delegation participating in the Joint Exercise of the People's Liberation Army and the People's Republic of China (PRC) for the Joint Exercise of the People's Liberation Army and the Vietnamese People's Liberation Army (PLAC-2021) returned safely to Guangxi Province of China, marking the successful completion of the seven-day exercise.
In this joint speech, the two militaries focused on the important topic of humanitarian medical rescue, closely aligned with the mission of the National Guard Rescue and Death Assistance Mission, and successfully improved the security capabilities of the two militaries by completing joint command, joint field rescue, batch wounded disposal, and so on, in accordance with practical standards.
The exercise results were acknowledged by both the Chinese and Vietnamese militaries.
Chairman of the Vietnamese Exercise Guidance Committee and Deputy Director-General of the Logistics Bureau of the Vietnam People’s Army, General Nguyen Hung Son, said at the closing ceremony that through the exercise, Vietnamese medical personnel have learned knowledge on exercise organization and professional activities from Chinese medical personnel and also seen the medical and support equipment of the Chinese side.
The results of the exercise demonstrated the professional capabilities of the military medical forces of both countries in medical assistance and epidemic prevention and control.
Chairman of China's Coordinating Group, Deputy Director of the Ministry of Health of Logistics and Security of the Central Military Commission, Chen Chunming, said that the exercise was a very important milestone in pioneering innovative practices based on the success of the Joint Diagnostic Exercise in 2018.
During the exercise, the People's Liberation Army of China donated medical protective masks, medical protective clothing, rapid nucleic acid testing instruments, and other health prevention materials to the Vietnamese People's Army.
